        <p>Those days are gone. and lone and sere, We linger in life's evening shade ; One loving voice alone to cheer, One willing hand alone to Yet still through mem'ry's wondrous power, Which never moves the heart in vain ; In many a restful, oniet hour, We live those early years again. Christmas Day, 1905.</p>
