      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>APRIL.</head>
        <p>APRIL.</p>
        <p>2.—Lora Milner took a public tarewell of Johannesburg.</p>
        <p>3.—Marylerione murder: Frank P. Hingham was, at tre Old Bailey. sentenced to death. s.—Britilicon: Mr. E. A. Villiers (L.), 8299; Mr. G. Loder 7392—majority, 817. (Mr. Loder appointed a Junior Lord of the Treasury). Canon E. Lyttelton elected Head Master of Harrow, Bloomsbury murder: Albert Bridgman was, at the Old Bailey, sentenced to death. 14.—Farewell banquet to Mr. Choate. At Harlesden Police- court Arthur Deve- reux, 3.5, chemist's assistant, who had been brought in the course of the day limn') Coventry, was remanded, charged with the murder of his wife and two children, whose bodies bad been found on the pre- Tinos day in a tin box which had been deposited at a fur- niture warehouse in the Harrow-I oad.</p>
        <p>way aeei dent near Huddersfield : Two persons killed, seven injured. 27.—Mr. Andrew Carnegie glace 000 000 to found a trust lend for the papeent of pensions to professors of edinintinnal institntions in the United Staten. Canada and Newlo indland.</p>
        <p>Selborne lett Englined for South Africa, to succeed Lewd Milner. MAY.</p>
        <p>1.---Destroyer Syren wrecked itn Eere Island No liyes lost. Eaatlnviske shock in Wales. 2.—Earl or Cliesterdeld robbed of jewels valued at Ella).</p>
        <p>6.—At the Old Bailey. thobroViers Stratton were sentenced to death for tlm De ptrord murders. strers airisesi in London ; the leader ejee:ed from the House or Coltmons, 13.—The King inspoeted new goP•s ittl presented Albert medals to Kollle of the survivtrs of the Dogger Bank incident, at Uuitittitmn hdace. 16.—King Alfonso of Spain appointed a General in the British Army. Lord Svlborne arnved at Cape Town. 17.—Lit. King appointed an lion. Admiral in the Spanish Navy. ()emir) yacht race for the Kaiser's Cup started from Sandy Honk. M.—Capt. Clad() dismissed the lloamian Navy. Ill.—Johann Hoch, the American illuebeard, senteneed to death for poi, ming his last wife. This notorious criminal had had many wiv(s who mysteriously disap- peared. Dock ap- pears to have, exer- cised an extraordi- nary influence over women, whc fell easy victims to his criminal mael.ina- tions. The trial caused great excite- ment in Chicago and throughout the United States. 20.—Lord Selborne sworn in as Governor of Orange River Colony. 22.--Riotous scenes in the House of Commons, the sitting being suspended. 23.—Lord E. Talbot. M.P., appointed a Lord of the Treasury and Junior Government whip. Execution of Alfred and Albert Stratton.</p>
